#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-led-neopixel.rst:4
#: 943937a33fa04e37bc27fc9047d5943b
msgid "NeoPixel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-led-neopixel.rst:8
#: 1fb1e22cafe242cabc5e8c96dfdc50cd
msgid "Up to four strings of \"NeoPixel\" style (WS2812B compatible) RGB LEDs can be used to display the same LED patterns as other RGB LEDs including those commonly installed on GPS/compass units.  Each string can have multiple LEDs with the maximum number dependent upon the autopilot's CPU speed.  On a high speed autopilot with an H7 processor, up to 44 individual LEDs per string are known to work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-led-neopixel.rst:10
#: 10195a3f87644a3b96b615ec65a9e46e
msgid "Attach each LED to a separate PWM output and set the following parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-led-neopixel.rst:12
#: 16d37c52d820485cb4fccae0b1050546
msgid "Set :ref:`NTF_LED_TYPES<NTF_LED_TYPES>` to include ``NeoPixel`` (bit 8)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-led-neopixel.rst:13
#: 9528fb62d5cc42ae888e6496b1dec7e4
msgid "Set :ref:`NTF_LED_LEN<NTF_LED_LEN>` to the number of LEDs connected to a servo output (up to 4)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-led-neopixel.rst:14
#: 9502a8b438154632887178d22ceac500
msgid "Set SERVOx_FUNCTION to ``NeoPixel1``, ``NeoPixel2``, ``NeoPixel3`` or ``NeoPixel4`` where \"x\" corresponds to the PWM output channel that the LED is connected to"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-led-neopixel.rst:16
#: 02a24db472d44caa87b5198897f16175
msgid "a few \"NeoPixel\" LED types have a different data order for the red and green data instead of the normal green/red/blue orde. If you are not displaying the desired colors, try setting the :ref:`NTF_LED_TYPES<NTF_LED_TYPES>` parameter to ``NeoPixelRGB`` tpe instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-led-neopixel.rst:18
#: b2c3b67101c7410d83ff58e09f8fe54c
msgid "Most WS2812 style LED and strings will operate correctly when connected to the autopilot. However, if you get intermittent or non-operation, you may need to implement one of the configurations below. This is due to the fact that the autopilot outputs swing to 3.3V but the worst case input signal high spec for the LED is 4.3V at a 5V supply. So at extremes of tolerance/manufacturing spec, you can get a combination which will not work correctly. In that case the easiest solution is to lower the LED supply voltage by inserting a silicon diode between the FCU 5V output and the LED 5V input, as shown below. Any silicon diode which can handle the current of the LED array can be used (for example, 1N4001 for 1A max). The cathode of the diode (marked with a gray stripe) must point toward the LED 5V input."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-serial-led-neopixel.rst:23
#: d0b58e96946542b9b27f8479c2d54627
msgid "But this causes a small loss in LED brilliance. An easy way to avoid this, if an LED can be isolated in the string, is to use an LED to level shift the signal for you so that the rest of the string can be powered by the full 5V."
msgstr ""
